at five a hunt for a good cause various  parks across clark county were filled  with tons of easter eggs today mary jane  belliesa takes us to desert horizons and  shares how one organization is raising  awareness on foster care  [Music]  dozens came out saturday morning in  support for saffie's easter egg hunt  safi which stands for specialized  alternatives for families and youth  provide therapeutic care to foster kids  in the system who need mental health  support kaitlyn johnson with safi says  this event is all about raising  awareness for that cause we decided that  we were going to hide one egg for every  child and teen that's been impacted by  foster care in clark county over the  last decade so that totaled 60 thousand  easter eggs  and then we also really wanted to drive  home the point of our kids are from all  over clark county so we chose 30 parks  all over clark county each egg contains  a qr code when scan provides you more  information on the organization how to  volunteer and donate and much more  jennifer chassero along with her two  kids say the egg hunt highlights an  important issue all while having fun at  the same time it means a lot to us  because actually wendell and jack bulls  got donations to um stuff the eggs and  they did a little drive  and so we  volunteered to  stuff the eggs and we actually went out  and hid all the eggs this morning and so  it was nice to see them  do  do something good for the community if  you weren't able to come out to the  event johnson says there are still  plenty of ways to support our foster  youth whether that's providing donations  monetary or items or volunteering at  things like this we always have  volunteer opportunities available on our  website so you can check that out at  sapphy.org  and then we also you can become a foster  parent or a respite parent mary jane  vallieza live local now  johnson says with an amazing turnout at  today's event across clark county they  anticipate to hold this event 